# Cloudflare Pages headers
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# Post-Lovable migration (2026-10-08):
#   - The Lovable build's dist/_headers already sets
#     `cache-control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable` on /assets/*
#     (content-hashed bundles, so the long cache is safe).
#   - Old sitetrace /js/*.js short-cache rule is removed: that path no longer
#     exists, and the new /assets/* has the correct long cache.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=()
  X-XSS-Protection: 0
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

# Compatibility: if a stale /js/* request lands on an old CDN node, keep it
# short so the user gets fresh content on the next visit.
/js/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate

/sitemap.xml
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
